WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:05.220
There's a lot to unpack in the latest Godzilla
flick's ending, from what the human characters

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:10.080
might do next to what this rapidly expanding
fictional universe could imply about the future

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.500
of the ancient beings known as Titans.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.520
Let's break it all down and explain the ending
of Godzilla: King of the Monsters.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.440
Monster spoilers ahead.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:24.040
Godzilla: King of the Monsters ends exactly
the way you'd expect it to: With a massive

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:29.529
Titan vs. Titan showdown in the ruins of Boston,
as Godzilla and Ghidorah battle it out for

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.180
apex predator status.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:35.780
The film ultimately reveals that Godzilla,
who seems to be working side by side with

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.820
humanity, has prevailed by showing us the
King of the Monsters chowing down on one of

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:44.360
Ghidorah's heads before blasting the remains
of the alien monster with his atomic breath.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.280
And then this exchange happens:

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.520
"Good thing he's on our side."

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:49.600
"For now."

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:54.600
It's an ominous postscript added by Monarch's
resident mythologist, who seems to understand

00:00:54.609 --> 00:00:58.809
that even though some version of a balance
has been achieved with Godzilla's victory,

00:00:58.809 --> 00:01:01.280
it could all go very wrong at any moment.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:06.100
The line "For now" might just seem like a
teaser for more sequels, but Dr. Chen's warning

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.100
speaks to the fragility of life on Earth in
the wake of the film.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:13.940
Everything old is new again, and that means
new rules for everyone that could be breaking

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.280
at any moment.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:20.420
Midway through the film, Godzilla managed
to chew off one of Ghidorah's heads before

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:24.180
the Oxygen Destroyer weapon was deployed and
rendered Godzilla dormant.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:29.400
Ghidorah was unaffected by the Destroyer because,
it turns out, he's an alien species who invaded

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.700
the Earth millennia ago.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:39.980
"A barren land laid to waste by the vile brute
known as...Monster Zero!"

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:44.740
Being an alien means he's also capable of
regrowing his head, but what about the original

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:45.740
noggin?

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:49.600
We have to wait until a post-credits scene
to find out what happened, but it turns out

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:53.820
that extra severed Ghidorah head was picked
up by fishermen and offered to Alan Jonah

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.500
and his eco-terrorist group.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:00.360
Jonah's original plan was to awaken the Titans
one at a time to "restore balance" to the

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:04.200
world, and that plan fell apart when Ghidorah
woke up all the Titans himself.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:07.720
So what can Jonah do with a Ghidorah head
that he couldn't do before?

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:12.840
Well, he could just be selling off the creature's
DNA as a valuable resource, or he could have

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.080
grander designs.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:19.100
A resurrected Ghidorah under the control of
a human master could change the game for all

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.900
Titans, and Jonah himself could be the King
of the Monsters.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:26.600
That's if he can manage to bring Monster Zero
back at all, and that's a big if.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.800
"So this plan is what you would call a long
shot."

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.020
"Well let's get started."

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:37.960
It's been a common feature of Godzilla films
for decades now that Mothra emerges as a benevolent,

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:41.800
self-sacrificing figure who wants to live
in harmony with humans rather than battle

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:45.320
them, and the Queen of the Monsters lived
up to that legacy in this film.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:50.980
After defeating Rodan, a weakened Mothra sacrificed
herself in battle against Ghidorah to help

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:54.260
Godzilla, with her essence falling on the
King of the Monsters to give him a little

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.920
added boost when he needed it.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:58.380
"Mothra can't die now."

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:04.100
Luckily, that's not the end of Mothra.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:08.920
News clippings in the film's closing credits
suggest the Queen is simply regenerating,

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.940
and will eventually emerge from another cocoon.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:15.240
The film also suggests that when she does
return, Mothra won't be alone.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:20.100
The Chen twins seem to be more than just two
scientists with an intense interest in monsters.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:24.860
Their devotion to Titans, plus their status
as twins, points to them being the MonsterVerse

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:29.630
version of the Shobijin, the twin fairies
in the original films who worship Mothra on

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:31.140
its home of Infant Island.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:33.900
We very likely haven't seen the last of them.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:39.100
Throughout the film we see references to Kong,
the king of Skull Island who was the star

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:42.720
of the second film in the MonsterVerse and
who will return again next year to battle

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:43.700
Godzilla.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:48.140
What we never actually see in the film is
anything new from Kong himself, even as Titans

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:50.840
around the world are waking up and responding
to Ghidorah.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:52.580
So why didn't Kong respond?

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:56.860
Well, the simple answer could just be that
he's on an island and isn't equipped to cross

00:03:56.860 --> 00:04:00.280
through the storms that surround it and make
his way across the ocean, but there may be

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.360
more to it.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:05.480
News clippings at the end of the film note
that Titans are making their way toward Skull

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:09.080
Island, seemingly setting the stage for Godzilla
vs. Kong.

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:13.960
If Kong is powerful enough to have resisted
Ghidorah's orders, that places him in rare

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:18.660
company alongside Mothra and Godzilla as one
of the strongest monsters on the planet.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:23.900
His absence is not a sign of weakness, but
a sign of strength…and, of course, a sequel.

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:29.540
Early in the film, Dr. Stanton theorizes that
Godzilla is able to move so quickly underwater

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:33.830
because the earth is, in fact, hollow, and
the Titan is using tunnels under oceans that

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:35.540
have yet to be discovered by man.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:40.220
His theory is laughed off, until the Monarch
team follows a dormant Godzilla into the depths

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:43.620
later in the film and discovers that there's
more than just tunnels.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:46.600
There's also an entire underwater city down
there.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:51.060
News clippings in the film's closing credits
reveal that this information has been made

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:54.860
public, and now the whole world knows that
"Hollow Earth Humans" once worshipped and

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.450
co-existed with The Titans.

00:04:56.450 --> 00:05:00.390
Of course, the underwater city we see in the
film was presumably destroyed by the nuclear

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:04.750
explosion that was set off to re-power Godzilla,
but if there really was a culture of people

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:09.100
worshipping "The First Gods," it's hard to
imagine that city was the only one.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:14.080
Even as the cities of the world are destroyed
by the Titans, Godzilla: King of the Monsters

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:16.949
also does its best to keep a human heart at
its center.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:20.820
Much of that heart centers on the Russell
family, which was torn apart by Godzilla's

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:22.920
battle in San Francisco in 2014.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:27.660
As the film goes on, Maddie has to watch her
mother, who was once her hero, become what

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:32.280
she calls "a monster" before earning redemption
by sacrificing herself in the fight to defeat

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:33.280
Ghidorah.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:36.200
"No sequel for you."

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:43.720
When the dust settles, Mark and Madison are
the only two members of the family left.

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:48.040
The film leaves their future open-ended, but
we already know Millie Bobby Brown will return

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:52.190
for Godzilla vs. Kong, so the Russells are
clearly planning to stick close to the Titans

00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:53.860
for at least a little while longer.

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:59.380
King of the Monsters spends most of its runtime
focusing on the title monster, Godzilla, and

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:04.220
three other key players among the Titans:
Ghidorah, Mothra, and Rodan.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:08.500
Despite what the trailers might suggest, though,
these creatures are far from the only Titans

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:09.280
in the film.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:14.140
Though we only glimpse a few of them, they
often seem to be creatures we've never seen

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:19.820
before in Godzilla films, most prominently
the giant spider Scylla and the mammoth creature

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:20.880
Behemoth.

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:26.020
But Monarch is never done searching, and the
revelation of alien Titans as well as underwater

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:28.360
cities leaves them with more places to look.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:32.699
The world of Titans is vast at the end of
the film, but there's always room to grow,

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:36.960
and we can probably expect more Titans to
emerge along with more sequels.

